{
  "kind": "lesson",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "transfer-fuse",
  "packId": "lawp.circuits.basics",
  "courseId": "first-contact",
  "moduleId": "the-loop",
  "title": "A fuse in another story",
  "skillIds": [
    "circuits.series.current"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 4,
  "taskRev": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Transfer\n\nSame physics, new cover. A garden lamp sits on the same series loop, and a fuse blows if current goes above **2**. You still want the lamp bright (`brightness` 2, which needs current at least 1) and you must keep the fuse. This lesson uses always-on constraints: blowing the fuse even once fails, even if you recover afterward.\n\nThis bites when you visit ohms `0.25` just to see. Current becomes `4`, the fuse blows, and the run is already lost. Curiosity that was safe in the first experiment is fatal here because the fuse remembers the overshoot. The story changed; the math did not.\n\n```text\nbattery → resistor → garden lamp → battery\nfuse blows if current > 2\n```\n\nA common mistake is repeating the first lesson's wander through every knob. The activity asks you to light the garden lamp brightly and never exceed current `2`. Go straight to ohms `1`. Do not visit `0.25`.\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "id": "garden-lamp",
      "kind": "experiment",
      "engine": "world-v1",
      "promptMd": "Light the garden lamp brightly. Do not blow the fuse (current ≤ 2).",
      "skillIds": [
        "circuits.series.current"
      ],
      "constraintMode": "always",
      "predict": {
        "promptMd": "If you pick ohms = 0.25, what happens to the fuse?",
        "kind": "mcq",
        "choices": [
          {
            "id": "ok",
            "md": "It stays fine"
          },
          {
            "id": "blow",
            "md": "It blows (current 4)"
          }
        ],
        "answer": "blow"
      },
      "world": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "id": "battery",
            "type": "battery",
            "props": {
              "cells": 1
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "resistor",
            "type": "resistor",
            "props": {
              "ohms": 2
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "lamp",
            "type": "lamp",
            "props": {
              "brightness": 1,
              "label": "Garden lamp"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "meter",
            "type": "meter",
            "props": {
              "current": 0.5
            }
          }
        ],
        "connections": [
          {
            "from": "battery",
            "to": "resistor"
          },
          {
            "from": "resistor",
            "to": "lamp"
          },
          {
            "from": "lamp",
            "to": "battery"
          }
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "id": "set-ohms",
            "label": "Set resistance",
            "target": "resistor",
            "op": "set",
            "key": "ohms",
            "values": [
              0,
              0.25,
              1,
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ],
        "rules": [
          {
            "id": "i-from-lookup",
            "when": [],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "meter",
                "key": "current",
                "value": {
                  "op": "div",
                  "a": "battery.cells",
                  "b": "resistor.ohms"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "bright-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "gte",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "dim-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "lt",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "view": {
          "kind": "graph",
          "assetMap": {}
        }
      },
      "goal": {
        "all": [
          {
            "path": "lamp.brightness",
            "op": "eq",
            "value": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        {
          "path": "meter.current",
          "op": "lte",
          "value": 2
        }
      ],
      "explainAfter": {
        "promptMd": "This lesson uses constraintMode always — blowing the fuse even once fails, even if you recover."
      },
      "misconceptionMap": [
        {
          "when": {
            "path": "meter.current",
            "op": "gt",
            "value": 2
          },
          "misconceptionId": "ignores-current-limit"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Same math as before. The fuse remembers."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Go straight to ohms = 1. Do not visit 0.25."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "Use the same current idea in a new story about a fuse."
}
